# Trace — configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you have:  cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is required to try Trace. `bun run dev` runs the whole agent with no credentials at
# all — seeded incidents, seeded collectors, and reasoning replayed from a genuinely captured
# Gemini response. Every variable below turns one more thing from replayed to real.
#
# Run from the REPO ROOT. Bun loads `.env` from the working directory while module resolution
# follows the file, so `cd apps/agent && bun run src/main.ts` starts cleanly and silently drops
# every credential in this file.


# ─── Caspian ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The comms layer, and the only variable `bun start` insists on. Free and instant from
# https://trycaspianai.com. Without it, use `bun run dev` instead.
CASPIAN_API_KEY=


# ─── Reasoning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset: reports are replayed from `packages/reasoner/recordings/`, similarity is computed by a
# deterministic lexical embedder, and free-form questions are declined (Trace says so rather than
# guessing). Set: live Gemini, with the recording kept behind it as a fallback for a 429 storm.
# Free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
#
# Note: free LLM tiers train on submitted prompts. Do not point one at real incident telemetry.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Defaults to gemini-2.5-flash. Only set this to try a different model.
# GEMINI_MODEL=


# ─── Channels ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# At least one channel must be connected or `bun start` exits. From @BotFather on Telegram.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Slack is off unless this is exactly `true`. The first start prints an install URL and a
# connection id; SAVE THAT ID BELOW. Without it every restart mints a brand-new connection, which
# orphans the previous install and invalidates the authorize_url you were about to click.
TRACE_ENABLE_SLACK=false
SLACK_CONNECTION_ID=

# Cosmetic, and applied only at install time — changing them later does not rename an existing app.
# TRACE_SLACK_DISPLAY_NAME=Trace
# TRACE_SLACK_ICON_URL=


# ─── Collectors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one real connector in this cut. BOTH are required: with either missing, the collector reports
# itself as a stated gap ("github was not consulted") rather than failing the investigation — and
# where a seeded stand-in covers it, the seed keeps answering instead.
# A classic read-only PAT with `repo` scope is enough. Repos are comma-separated `owner/name`.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# TRACE_GITHUB_REPOS=your-org/payments-api,your-org/checkout-web


# ─── Storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset: in-memory, nothing persists across a restart. That is a real implementation held to the
# same contract suite as Postgres, not a stand-in.
# Set: Postgres. Migrations run automatically on connect, so `docker compose up -d` and then
# `bun start` is the whole setup.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://trace:trace@localhost:5433/trace

# The tenant a single-tenant deploy files everything under. Leave unset for the built-in default.
# Must be a UUID; Trace refuses to start otherwise. CHANGING THIS AFTER DATA EXISTS hides every
# investigation already stored — the rows survive, and every read filters them out.
# TRACE_ORG_ID=

# Opts the Postgres contract suite into `bun test`. Unset, those tests skip and the suite stays
# credential-free and runs in milliseconds. Point it at a scratch database, not a real one.
# TRACE_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://trace:trace@localhost:5433/trace


# ─── Proactive alerting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only path where Trace speaks first, so it is off unless an operator BOTH opens a port and
# names recipients. An alerting system POSTs {system, id, summary, firedAt?} to the port; Trace
# reconstructs the incident and pages the rotation with the finding already in hand, once per
# incident.
#
# With the port open and this list empty, Trace still investigates and simply pages nobody.
#
# Recipients are comma-separated addresses for whichever *active* connection will send — a Telegram
# chat id, a Slack user id, an email address. An unreachable one is logged and the rest of the
# rotation still gets paged.
# TRACE_ALERT_PORT=8787
# TRACE_ONCALL_RECIPIENTS=
